  "No example has been reviewed by a person. machine_checked means the label's premises were checked mechanically (inventory codes, bundle facts, an independent re-application of spec 06 §3); it is not a legal review.",
  "Split rule: adversarial_holdout for every example with an adversarial class; otherwise, for the examples created 2026-10-19, dev when int(sha256(id)[:8], 16) % 10 < 4, else test. The 13 examples created 2026-10-20 (ids ver-dev-*, tmp-dev-*) were written for dev, with case templates no test or adversarial_holdout example uses. There is no train split in v0.",
  "Paths under files are relative to this directory; dependency paths are relative to experiments/waymaker-ai.",
  "2026-10-20 (align-bench): labels aligned with the spec 06/07 rules decided 2026-10-20; every changed label has revision+1 and a revision_history entry naming the rule. 13 non-adversarial legal items were added to dev (8 citation_verification, 5 temporal_version_selection) with their own case templates. Both owned bundles are at bundle_version 2 (structure_complete on every provision).",
  "Every example carries scenario.case_template. Variants written from one case (translations, re-dated or re-anchored variants, the same claim with a different citation or scope) share a template. case_templates.shared_by_dev_and_an_eval_split lists the templates that straddle dev and test/adversarial_holdout because v0 was split per example (hash rule) before templates existed; they were reported, not re-split."
 ],
